id: pm-gh1780
title: "GH-1780: the runRegisteredCommandForTest doc says undeclared option keys pass through, but the harness refuses them with unknown_option on a command that declares flags"
description: "GH-1780 (filed 2026-11-24 by the package-fleet maintainer after the 2026.11.14 to 2026.11.2x migration). The JSDoc of runRegisteredCommandForTest (bound as harness.runCommand) in src/sdk/testing.ts, published in dist/sdk/testing.d.ts, ends its option contract with 'and undeclared keys pass through'. Since the host alignment of pm-gh1726/pm-gh1727 the direct-caller normalizer (normalizeDirectExtensionCommandOptions) refuses a key that is neither a declared spelling nor a host-owned option with unknown_option (exit 2) before dispatch, on every extension-created command path that declares flags. Undeclared keys still pass through in three cases only: a command that declares no flags (pm-4of199 owns that refusal), a hand-built registry with no flag registrations, and a native core command path an extension extends or overrides. An array for a scalar flag is refused with extension_flag_value_invalid. Reproduced on 2026.11.25 by reading the normalizer: refuseUnknownExtensionOption runs for every non-host key when declaredDefinitions is non-empty and the policy is refuse. docs/SDK.md repeats the sentence for the harness but correctly scopes hand-built registries. Fleet impact (from the report): the largest single failure class of the migration, about 25 suites across pm-slack-standup, pm-todos, pm-github, pm-brief, pm-context and pm-screen; the refusal read like a harness bug. Duplicate check: searched runCommand undeclared option pass through unknown_option harness; pm-gh1665 (closed) shipped the normalizer, pm-4of199 (open) owns zero-flag refusal, pm-gh1731 and pm-gh1657 own migration notes and SDK release-note lines."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[6]: agent-ux,docs,extensions,"gh:1780",sdk,testing
created_at: "2026-11-25T05:50:53.377Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-25T07:15:56.793Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-25T07:15:55.479Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-25T07:15:55.479Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: "The runRegisteredCommandForTest JSDoc and the docs/SDK.md harness paragraph state the current rule: undeclared keys are refused with unknown_option before dispatch on a command that declares flags, exactly as the CLI refuses an unknown flag, and an array for a scalar flag is refused with extension_flag_value_invalid; Both texts name the three cases that still pass undeclared keys through (zero-flag command, hand-built registry, native core path) and the supported way to unit-test a handler with a free option bag; A harness test pins each documented case so the text cannot drift from behaviour again"
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: low
confidence: high
reporter: unbraind
severity: medium
resolution: "Rewrote the runRegisteredCommandForTest JSDoc (published in dist/sdk/testing.d.ts) and the docs/SDK.md harness paragraph: on a command that declares flags an undeclared key is refused with unknown_option (exit 2) before the handler runs, exactly as the CLI refuses an unknown flag, and an array for a non-list flag with extension_flag_value_invalid; reserved host keys pass unchanged; undeclared keys pass verbatim only for a zero-flag command (pm-4of199), a hand-built registry and a native core path an extension extends. Both texts say how to unit-test a handler with a free option bag (call the handler directly). A harness-parity case pins every documented case."
expected_result: Extension authors reading the harness contract learn the shipped refusal rule and its exceptions
actual_result: "The JSDoc and SDK.md state the rule and the three exceptions; the new harness-parity test pins the GH-1780 reproduction, the array refusal, host-key pass-through and both pass-through cases"
